  "body": "Part of #720 (sub-issue). Case study: [docs/case-studies/issue-720](https://github.com/link-assistant/router/blob/issue-720-99e7abc4e6c1/docs/case-studies/issue-720/README.md).\n\n## Summary\nRouter's model catalog is compiled into the binary and governed by `docs/model-truth-contract.md`; a vendor rename needs a release. CLIProxyAPI fetches catalog documents from configurable `models.sources` (catalog, codex-catalog, devin-catalog), refreshes them every 3 hours and reloads on change (v8.0.14\u201315).\n\nCase study: `docs/case-studies/issue-720/solution-plans.md` \u00a7 O.\n\n## Proposal\n1. `MODEL_CATALOG_SOURCES` (comma-separated URLs or file paths) merged over the compiled catalog with documented precedence; documents validated against the model-truth JSON Schema; invalid documents are rejected with the compiled catalog kept.\n2. `MODEL_CATALOG_REFRESH_SECS` (default 10800); failed fetches keep the last good catalog and are logged once per source.\n3. `--local-model name=provider:upstream` equivalent for ad-hoc entries.\n4. `GET /api/management/routing/model-definitions/{channel}` returns the effective catalog per provider.\n\n## Tests\nSchema rejection; merge precedence; refresh with a controllable clock; failed fetch keeps previous catalog; catalog URL subject to `UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_NETWORKS`; size cap enforced.\n\n## Prior art\nCLIProxyAPI `internal/registry/*_test.go`, `models.sources` in `config.example.yaml`.\n\n## Security\nCatalog URLs go through the SSRF guard; documents are size-capped; a catalog entry can never widen a token's subscription policy.\n\n## Compatibility\nUnset sources mean the compiled catalog exactly as today.\n",
